## 🔹 PART 9 — MIGRATIONS & SUPERUSER

### Step 21 — Run migrations

Migrations are how Django creates and updates database tables based on your Python models.
Always run these commands when you first set up a project or after changing a model:

```bash
python manage.py makemigrations
python manage.py migrate
```

> - `makemigrations` — looks at your models and generates migration files (like a plan)
> - `migrate` — actually applies those plans and creates/updates the database tables
>
> ⚠️ **Rule:** Always run `migrate` before creating a superuser. The superuser depends
> on the auth tables that migrate creates.

### Step 22 — Create a superuser

```bash
python manage.py createsuperuser
```

You'll be prompted to enter:
- **Username:** (e.g. `admin` or your name)
- **Email:** Optional — just press Enter to skip
- **Password:** Type it (it won't show — this is normal for security)

Once done, you can log into the admin panel at: **http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/**

