```

> **Why one form template for both Create and Update?**
> Both pages use the same HTML structure. The only difference is what the `action`
> variable says ("Create" or "Update"), which the view passes in.
> This is the DRY principle — Don't Repeat Yourself.
>
> **What is `{% csrf_token %}`?** A security measure. Django requires this inside every
> `POST` form to prevent cross-site forgery attacks. Never forget it or your form won't submit.

