## 🔹 PART 11 — DJANGO EXTRAS (Messages, Filters, Humanize)

### Messages (Flash Alerts)

Flash messages show one-time alerts to the user after an action (like "Item saved!").
They automatically disappear after the page refreshes.

**How to send a message in a view:**
```python
from django.contrib import messages

messages.success(request, 'Done! Item was saved.')
messages.error(request, 'Something went wrong.')
messages.warning(request, 'Watch out — this is a warning.')
messages.info(request, 'Just so you know...')
```

> The `{{ message.tags }}` in base.html automatically picks up the Tailwind classes
> you mapped in `settings.py` and applies them to the alert box.

---

### Template Filters (Quick Reference)

Template filters transform the value of a variable before displaying it.
Use them with a pipe `|` symbol directly in your HTML.

```django
{# Shorten text by words #}
{{ item.description|truncatewords:15 }}
→ "This is a sample description that has been..."

{# Shorten text by characters #}
{{ item.title|truncatechars:30 }}
→ "My Long Title That Gets Cut Off..."

{# Uppercase / Lowercase / Title Case #}
{{ item.title|upper }}    → "MY ITEM TITLE"
{{ item.title|lower }}    → "my item title"
{{ item.title|title }}    → "My Item Title"

{# Count items in a list #}
{{ items|length }}        → 5

{# Auto plural — adds "s" when count is not 1 #}
{{ items|length }} item{{ items|length|pluralize }}
→ "1 item" or "5 items"

{# Format date #}
{{ item.created_at|date:"Y-m-d" }}    → "2026-01-15"
{{ item.created_at|date:"D, d M Y" }} → "Wed, 15 Jan 2026"
```

---

### Humanize (Human-Friendly Text)

Humanize gives you natural language formatting for dates and numbers.

Make sure `'django.contrib.humanize'` is in `INSTALLED_APPS` (we added it in Part 3).

Then load it in any template where you need it:

```html
{% load humanize %}

<!-- Relative time — perfect for "posted X ago" -->
{{ item.created_at|naturaltime }}
→ "3 minutes ago" / "2 days ago"

<!-- Add commas to large numbers -->
{{ price|intcomma }}
→ 1,000,000

<!-- Natural day -->
{{ item.created_at|naturalday }}
→ "today" / "yesterday" / "Jan 15"
```

